# This repo is worked on from Windows but its scripts run on an ARM Linux
# alarm panel and in WSL. A CR breaks them invisibly, so force LF on checkout
# regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.example       text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
rc.local        text eol=lf
tuxedo-upload.sh text eol=lf
# patches.tsv was NOT covered, and it is the file that can least afford it. Its
# parser is field-and-whitespace sensitive, and apply-patches.py and
# verify-panel.sh both read it -- a trailing CR lands in the last field of every
# row. The committed blob has always been LF, so nothing was ever published
# wrong; but `git checkout` on Windows rewrote the working copy as CRLF and
# ci/checks.sh then reported "FAIL patch table well formed" with
# offset-not-hex, not-lowercase-hex and stock-equals-patched, on a table that
# had not changed. A checkout broke the check, not an edit.
*.tsv           text eol=lf

# Firmware images and binaries.
*.hdr           binary
*.bin           binary
*.jffs2         binary
*.hex           binary
evidence/*.log -text
image/** text eol=lf
evidence/* -text
tools/** text eol=lf
probe/** text eol=lf
